IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act -- piece cp4 (section 55.2(5.2) to section 66.1): THE NOUNS this piece shares.
--
-- Declarations only; no rules, no assertions. The other cp4 modules import this one.
-- Every type name starts with "cp4" because it is not a term the Act defines in this piece's range
-- (NOTES.md of the keel, "Naming conventions"); every field and constructor is worded to be unique
-- once all pieces sit in one folder.
-- Money is a NUMBER of Canadian dollars; a rate is a fraction; a month is the DATE of its first day.

§ `cp4 -- shared vocabulary`

§§ `The three portions of a contributor's retirement pension`

-- Sections 56(1)(b), 58(2) and 65.1(9) split a retirement pension into three portions: the portion for
-- the base contributions (paragraph 46(1)(a)), the portion for the first additional contributions
-- (paragraph 46(1)(b)) and the portion for the second additional contributions (paragraph 46(1)(c)).
-- Section 46 is in piece cp3, so the amounts are supplied; each is a monthly amount in dollars.
-- src:1623 | (b) 75% of the amount of the contributor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as the aggregate of
-- src:1624 | (i) the amount calculated as provided in subsection (3),
-- src:1625 | (ii) the amount calculated as provided in subsection (3.1), and
-- src:1626 | (iii) the amount calculated as provided in subsection (3.2).
@ref Act s 56(1)(b) (src:1623-1626)
DECLARE `cp4 Retirement pension portions` HAS
    `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension` IS A NUMBER
    `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension` IS A NUMBER
    `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension` IS A NUMBER
